== 3.9 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Farming in which the produce is mainly for the farmer's family is called],
  [subsistence farming],
  [mixed farming],
  [commercial farming],
  [plantation farming]
)

#mcq(2, [Farming with little labour and capital per hectare is],
  [horticultural],
  [plantation],
  [intensive],
  [extensive]
)

#mcq(3, [Shifting cultivation depends on],
  [mechanisation],
  [irrigation],
  [heavy fertiliser use],
  [a fallow period that restores fertility]
)

#mcq(4, [Shifting cultivation breaks down when],
  [the crop is sold],
  [the land is irrigated],
  [population pressure shortens the fallow],
  [the farmer buys fertiliser]
)

#mcq(5, [A plantation is characterised by],
  [one crop, capital, hired labour and processing nearby],
  [many crops for the family],
  [communal ownership only],
  [seasonal hunting]
)

#mcq(6, [Cocoa is best grown in areas with],
  [frost in winter],
  [over 1 500 mm of rain and a long wet season],
  [a long dry season],
  [under 500 mm of rain]
)

#mcq(7, [Groundnut is best suited to the],
  [savanna belt],
  [rain forest],
  [coastal lagoon],
  [mangrove swamp]
)

#mcq(8, [Millet and sorghum are grown chiefly in the],
  [mangrove],
  [Sudan savanna and Sahel],
  [rain forest],
  [derived savanna]
)

#mcq(9, [Rice in Nigeria is grown mainly],
  [in the mangrove],
  [in river valleys and irrigated schemes],
  [on the coastal sand],
  [on the high plateau]
)

#mcq(10, [Yam and cassava are typical of the],
  [Sahel],
  [Sudan savanna],
  [forest and derived savanna],
  [montane zone]
)

#mcq(11, [Nomadic pastoralism is a system of],
  [fishing in the deep sea],
  [planting trees],
  [livestock herding that moves with pasture and water],
  [growing one cash crop]
)

#mcq(12, [Ranching differs from nomadic pastoralism because ranching],
  [uses no land],
  [fences the herd and grows its feed],
  [moves every week],
  [keeps only poultry]
)

#mcq(13, [Inland fishing in Nigeria takes place in],
  [the desert],
  [the deep Atlantic],
  [rivers, lakes and fish ponds],
  [the mangrove canopy]
)

#mcq(14, [The main post-harvest problem of Nigerian agriculture is],
  [too much fertiliser],
  [excess rainfall],
  [too many tractors],
  [inadequate storage and processing]
)

#mcq(15, [The main physical problem of Nigerian agriculture is],
  [a shortage of land],
